    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The closing of once-active spaces of collaboration marks the end of an era. Office locations in Reno and Woodland Hills, sites of a broken professional bond, are undergoing location shutdown. This organizational change is part of a strategic re-alignment of loyalties, as the entity severing ties seeks to co-locate teams. The physical dissolution of bonds is complete, leaving only the memory of communal spaces now lost.",
